% Section 3
(3. Supported 10-Class Dermatological Pathology Taxonomy) 265 drawSectionHeader

/Helvetica findfont 8.5 scalefont setfont
0.2 0.25 0.3 setrgbcolor
45 238 moveto (1. Eczema (Class 0): Acute/subacute erythematous spongiotic patches with microvesiculation and pruritus.) show
45 224 moveto (2. Warts & Molluscum (Class 1): Hyperkeratotic verrucous papules with punctate black thrombosed capillary dots.) show
45 210 moveto (3. Melanoma (Class 2): Malignant melanocytic neoplasm assessed via ABCDE asymmetric contour & variegation.) show
45 196 moveto (4. Atopic Dermatitis (Class 3): Chronic flexural xerosis with lichenification in antecubital and popliteal fossae.) show
45 182 moveto (5. Basal Cell Carcinoma (Class 4): Pearly translucent nodule with telangiectasia and rolled active borders.) show
45 168 moveto (6. Melanocytic Nevi (Class 5): Benign symmetric pigment macules with uniform melanin distribution.) show
45 154 moveto (7. Benign Keratosis (Class 6): Solar lentigines, seborrheic verrucous crusts, and benign lichenoid keratoses.) show
45 140 moveto (8. Psoriasis & Lichen Planus (Class 7): Well-demarcated salmon plaques with thick micaceous silvery scales.) show
45 126 moveto (9. Seborrheic Keratoses (Class 8): Stuck-on waxy hyperkeratotic lesions with prominent keratin pseudocysts.) show
45 112 moveto (10. Tinea / Ringworm / Candidiasis (Class 9): Advancing annular erythematous ring with distinct central clearing.) show

